{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0c1fcc85c5704ee9016a90331ae96887d285be26d3a5606731","text":"I’m going to inspect the orchestrator-provided bundle first, focusing on the workspace state model, UI rendering path, and existing harness tests. After that I’ll submit one focused patch with the feature test and implementation together so the shared worktree stays buildable.","phase":"commentary","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null},"threadId":"01a04347-4439-7793-843e-fa41147c6505","turnId":"01a04347-743e-7a41-b378-5cca090cd6b0","completedAtMs":1787835164067},"emittedAtMs":1787835164068}
{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_4bo2H2Veq7ztYyKNr9O7xVda","pluginId":null,"scriptPath":null,"command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"''^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent\" /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/context-bundles/orchestrator-1815816-0/bundle-2.md'","cwd":"/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/repo","processId":"69720","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"inProgress","commandActions":[{"type":"search","command":"rg -n '^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent' /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/context-bundles/orchestrator-1815816-0/bundle-2.md","query":"^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent","path":"bundle-2.md"}],"aggregatedOutput":null,"exitCode":null,"durationMs":null},"threadId":"01a04347-4439-7793-843e-fa41147c6505","turnId":"01a04347-743e-7a41-b378-5cca090cd6b0","startedAtMs":1787835166267},"emittedAtMs":1787835166268}
{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_4bo2H2Veq7ztYyKNr9O7xVda","pluginId":null,"scriptPath":null,"command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"''^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent\" /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/context-bundles/orchestrator-1815816-0/bundle-2.md'","cwd":"/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/repo","processId":"69720","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"search","command":"rg -n '^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent' /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/context-bundles/orchestrator-1815816-0/bundle-2.md","query":"^(#|##|###)|Review|review|patch|highlight|done|yes|no|close|closed|agent|chat|TerminalUi|UiHarness|WorkLeafController|Agent","path":"bundle-2.md"}],"aggregatedOutput":"1:# Work Leaf Context Bundle\n35:# Work Leaf Architecture\n40:## Public Crate Surface\n43:agent-provider integrations use:\n45:- `agent` and `agent_runtime` define provider-neutral agent domain types and runtime contracts.\n47:- `cli` defines the command-chat API used by the binary and by controller orchestration.\n51:- `orchestrator`, `patch`, `review`, `linearize`, and `locks` define core workflow behavior.\n57:- UI integration: `WorkLeafController`, `WorkLeafSnapshot`, `WorkLeafSession`, `WorkLeafEvent`,\n59:- Agent-provider integration: `AgentBackend`, `AgentStreamEvent`, `AgentShutdownHandle`,\n60:  `AgentProfile`, `AgentKind`, `AgentLaunch`, `AgentSession`, `AgentId`, `ChatMessage`,\n61:  `MessageRole`, `PromptPolicy`, `ReadPermission`, `AgentError`.\n65:- Core workflows: `AgentOrchestrator`, `GitPatcher`, `PatchCoordinator`, `GitHistory`,\n66:  `ReviewCoordinator`, `LinearizePlanner`, `FileLockTable`.\n67:- Terminal UI: `TerminalApp`, `RemoteTerminalApp`, `TerminalUi`, `UiHarness`, `UiAction`, `UiKey`,\n68:  `UiMode`, `UiSurface`, `PaneFocus`, `AgentListEntry`.\n70:## Layering\n74:1. Provider-neutral domain and runtime contracts live in `src/agent.rs` and\n75:   `src/agent_runtime.rs`.\n76:2. Core workflows live in `src/cli.rs`, `src/orchestrator.rs`, `src/patch.rs`, `src/review.rs`,\n81:The dependency direction is inward. UIs drive `WorkLeafController`; the controller drives\n82:`CommandChat`; `CommandChat` drives the active `AgentBackend` and the workflow coordinators. Core\n83:workflow modules do not depend on terminal rendering, terminal input, or a specific agent provider.\n87:`WorkLeafController<CodexBackend>`, and exposes that controller through\n94:daemon. A CLI-managed daemon receives `WORK_LEAF_PARENT_PID`, does not inherit the terminal file\n103:listen address when a caller needs an explicit override; the script does not fall back to another\n106:## Agent Domain\n108:`src/agent.rs` owns provider-neutral agent data:\n110:- `AgentId` validates stable agent identifiers.\n111:- `AgentKind` identifies the provider kind. `AgentKind::Codex` is the built-in provider, and\n112:  `AgentKind::External(String)` identifies non-Codex providers.\n113:- `AgentProfile` carries the active provider kind, display name, and default feature label.\n114:- `AgentLaunch` describes a new agent session request.\n115:- `AgentSession` stores the agent id, kind, feature, state, messages, and modified files.\n117:- `PromptPolicy` injects project instructions and worktree access rules into agent prompts.\n119:  filesystem reads while keeping writes mediated by patches.\n120:- `AgentError` is the shared error type for launch, send, and prompt policy failures.\n122:`src/agent.rs` also re-exports `AgentBackend`, `AgentStreamEvent`, and `AgentShutdownHandle` from\n123:`src/agent_runtime.rs`, so callers can import all provider-neutral agent interfaces from\n124:`work_leaf::agent`.\n126:## Agent Runtime Interface\n128:`src/agent_runtime.rs` owns the provider-neutral backend contract:\n130:- `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.\n131:- `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.\n132:- `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a\n133:  sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.\n134:- `AgentBackend::shutdown_handle` returns an `AgentShutdownHandle` for terminating active provider\n136:- `AgentStreamEvent` carries status text, streamed agent messages, and streamed errors.\n137:- `AgentShutdownHandle::shutdown` terminates registered processes, waits briefly, and then kills\n140:The runtime also contains provider-process support that is not part of the public provider API:\n146:New agent providers implement `AgentBackend`; they do not add provider logic to `src/codex.rs`.\n151:`AgentShutdownHandle` registry.\n153:## Codex Provider\n155:`src/codex.rs` contains the Codex-specific implementation of the neutral agent runtime interface:\n159:- `CodexBackend` stores Codex session history and implements `AgentBackend`.\n162:  `PromptPolicy`; resumed invocations for known sessions pass only the follow-up message because the\n167:  identifiers for resume and to convert agent message, error, and status events into\n168:  `AgentStreamEvent` values. The parser accepts standard JSON whitespace around field separators\n171:`CodexBackend` is a provider implementation, not the owner of the generic agent contract. Callers\n172:that need provider-neutral behavior import `AgentBackend` from `work_leaf::agent` or from the\n173:top-level re-export, not from `work_leaf::codex`.\n175:## Command Chat\n178:tests. It is generic over `B: AgentBackend`.\n183:- active `AgentProfile`,\n184:- agent sessions and generated agent ids,\n185:- orchestrator, patch, review, and linearizer coordination,\n187:- backend shutdown through `AgentShutdownHandle`.\n191:- `CommandChat::new` for constructing command chat state with a backend.\n192:- `CommandChat::with_agent_profile` for selecting a non-default provider profile.\n193:- `CommandChat::handle_line` for processing command lines such as `new`, `chat`, `review`, and\n195:- `CommandChat::prepare_agent_launch`, `launch_prepared_agent_streaming`, and\n196:  `launch_prepared_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven launch flows.\n197:- `CommandChat::send_to_agent`, `send_to_agent_streaming`, and\n198:  `send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven message flows.\n199:- `CommandChat::shutdown_agents` and `shutdown_handle` for lifecycle cleanup.\n201:`CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.\n202:Workflow code must not hard-code `AgentKind::Codex` when the active profile supplies the provider.\n204:## UI-Neutral Controller\n206:`src/workspace.rs::WorkLeafController<B>` is the preferred API for frontends. It owns UI-neutral\n213:- LLM-generated chat titles through hidden `title-<agent-id>` backend launches, with\n214:  `src/chat_title.rs::ChatTitleAgent` tracking first-prompt naming state,\n216:- background launch/send/review workers,\n217:- stream routing from `AgentStreamEvent` into the selected session,\n218:- review startup, automatic per-patch-agent review routing, reviewer-session creation, and\n219:  reviewed-commit bookkeeping,\n220:- shutdown propagation to running agents.\n222:When an agent worker finishes, the controller records the agent output and clears that session's\n223:loading state. A user-agent response becomes review-ready only when the orchestrator transcript shows\n224:an applied patch from that agent and the agent emits `@work-leaf done`. Successful patch application\n225:returns a continuation prompt to the patch agent when the agent has not reported done, so the agent can\n226:run repository-required checks through locked command directives, provide follow-up patches, or signal\n227:review readiness. Repository build, test, format, and required-check commands run only through\n228:agent-emitted orchestrator directives that name the command and the write-lock paths the command may\n231:instruction files into agent prompts, and the active backend agent is responsible for choosing and\n232:requesting the repository checks required by those instructions before reporting work done.\n233:Tracked file changes produced by locked commands remain pending for that patch agent until the agent\n234:commits them through the patch protocol or reverts them. Pending command changes block\n235:`@work-leaf done`, and the orchestrator returns the tracked diff so the agent can submit the command\n236:output as a provisional patch when it belongs in the final work.\n238:Review bookkeeping has three scopes. The controller records a launch-time review baseline for each\n239:patch agent, tracks the latest reviewed hash for that patch agent so the same agent head is not\n240:reviewed twice, and asks reviewers to inspect every provisional commit from the active baseline\n241:through the latest patch-agent commit. `CommandChat` also keeps the ordered exact review targets that\n242:completed review during the active instance, and those targets form the linearizer handoff. This lets\n243:one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier\n244:reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.\n246:The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That\n247:system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command\n248:lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching\n249:one or more user agents. Multi-agent launch requests dispatch `new [prompt...]` once per requested\n250:agent through the same controller paths used by command-mode input.\n254:- `WorkLeafController::new` to wrap a `CommandChat<B>`.\n258:- `create_agent` to reserve, select, and launch an agent session from a prompt.\n259:- `send_command_agent_message` to route chat from the Work Leaf command surface to `command-agent`.\n261:- `start_review` to create or resume reviewer sessions for explicit history-wide review and stream\n262:  reviewer output.\n269:- `WorkLeafSession`, which contains agent id, kind, feature/title, transcript lines, and loading\n275:`WorkLeafEvent` uses append-oriented transcript events for efficient remote frontends. `AgentAdded`\n276:provides the initial session snapshot, `AgentLineAppended` carries one new session line, and\n277:`CommandTranscriptLine` carries one new command transcript line. `AgentStatusUpdated` carries\n278:session metadata and loading state without re-sending the session transcript. `AgentUpdated` remains\n280:appends and status changes are not paired with full-session replacement events, so remote frontends\n283:New UIs should consume `WorkLeafController` and these DTOs. They should not duplicate worker\n284:spawning, session naming, review lookup, loading bookkeeping, or orchestrator event routing.\n286:## Localhost HTTP Controller\n288:`src/http_controller.rs::HttpControllerServer` is a transport adapter over `WorkLeafController`. It\n289:owns no workflow behavior; each HTTP route delegates to the corresponding controller method or DTO:\n294:- `POST /command` calls `WorkLeafController::execute_command_line`.\n295:- `POST /command-agent` calls `WorkLeafController::send_command_agent_message`.\n296:- `POST /agent/message` calls `WorkLeafController::send_message`.\n297:- `POST /agent/interrupt` calls `WorkLeafController::interrupt_agent`.\n298:- `POST /transcript` calls `WorkLeafController::push_transcript_line`.\n299:- `POST /loading-text` calls `WorkLeafController::loading_text`.\n300:- `POST /shutdown` calls `WorkLeafController::shutdown` and stops the daemon loop.\n303:serializes and deserializes the same workspace DTOs used by in-process frontends. `AgentId`\n304:deserialization uses `src/agent.rs::AgentId::new`, so HTTP payloads preserve the same identifier\n307:## Terminal UI\n312:direct `WorkLeafController<B>` calls for in-process use. `src/terminal_app.rs::RemoteTerminalApp`\n315:`TerminalUi`, and render from the cache rather than fetching a full controller snapshot for every\n318:rendering invalidation, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends chat text to the selected\n319:agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is selected. Bracketed-paste\n320:newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits the buffered chat text.\n321:When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the chat buffer with\n322:`/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat\n325:The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading\n326:state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready\n327:state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy\n330:`src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:\n333:- `AgentListEntry` is the terminal left-pane representation of an agent row.\n335:- `TerminalUi` renders left/right panes, prompts, cursor placement, command-interface selection, and\n336:  terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets\n339:`src/ui_harness.rs::UiHarness` is the test harness for terminal behavior. It exercises the same\n340:`TerminalUi` frame path used by the interactive example. UI tests should drive\n341:`UiHarness::handle_byte` or `UiHarness::handle_bytes` rather than duplicating terminal input logic.\n343:A web UI, desktop UI, or non-terminal integration should not depend on `TerminalApp` or\n344:`TerminalUi`; it should depend on `WorkLeafController` and the DTOs in `src/workspace.rs`.\n346:## Core Workflow Modules\n348:`src/orchestrator.rs::AgentOrchestrator<B>` parses and executes `@work-leaf` directives emitted by\n349:agents. It uses `FileLockTable` for file reads and command write locks, `CommandWritePolicy` for\n350:command classification, `PatchCoordinator` for patch requests, and the active `AgentBackend` for\n353:`src/locks.rs::FileLockTable` owns root-scoped path normalization and read/write locking.\n355:heuristic read-only/write-intent classification for commands when an agent is unsure. Agent-requested\n356:command runs execute in the project root while `FileLockTable` holds write locks for the normalized\n357:lock paths supplied by the agent. File paths are normalized relative to the project root and cannot\n360:`src/patch.rs::GitPatcher` validates and applies unified diffs under write locks and creates\n361:metadata commits for accepted patches. It also accepts a matching already-applied diff when a locked\n363:agent's provisional patch. `PatchCoordinator<B>` connects patch conflicts and malformed patch\n364:diagnostics back to the active agent backend. `PatchRequest`, `PatchOutcome`, and `PatchError` are\n365:the public patch workflow types.\n367:`src/review.rs::GitHistory` reads latest agent commits from repository history, builds cumulative\n368:review targets for a patch agent since a launch or reviewed baseline, and resolves agent metadata\n369:commits by exact hash. `ReviewCoordinator<B>` launches reviewer agents against those review targets\n370:and loops until the reviewer reports no findings or the configured maximum round count is reached.\n371:`CommandChat` resolves reviewer `@work-leaf` directives, such as file reads, before interpreting\n372:reviewer output as findings. `CommandChat` and `WorkLeafController` keep a stable\n373:`review-<agent-id>` reviewer identity for each patch agent and skip latest agent heads that have\n374:already completed review. `AgentCommit`, `ReviewResult`, and `ReviewError` are the public review\n375:workflow types. `WorkLeafController` scopes automatic review after a patch agent reports done to the\n376:patch agent that produced the provisional commit; explicit review commands use the history-wide\n377:review target lookup.\n380:agent with decisions, groups, and required tests. `LinearizeAction`, `LinearizeGroup`,\n382:linearization workflow types. `CommandChat` and `WorkLeafController` launch linearization from the\n383:exact commits recorded as reviewed in the current command-chat or controller instance; unrelated\n384:historical agent metadata commits are outside the linearizer scope unless the user explicitly reviews\n385:or adds them in that session. When one patch-agent id completes multiple reviewed commits in one\n386:active instance, each reviewed hash is listed independently for the linearizer.\n389:for agent launch prompts.\n391:`src/chat_title.rs` is crate-private. It builds the prompt used for hidden chat-title backend\n395:## Extension Rules\n400:2. Wrap it in `WorkLeafController<B>`.\n407:`WorkLeafController`; new workflow behavior still belongs in the owning workflow or controller\n410:New agent-provider support follows this path:\n412:1. Define an `AgentProfile` with `AgentKind::External`.\n413:2. Implement `AgentBackend` for the provider.\n415:4. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.\n416:5. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.\n417:6. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.\n420:only translate user input into controller calls and render controller snapshots. Agent providers\n423:## API and Architecture Change Policy\n427:surfaces for UIs, agent providers, command orchestration, and core workflows. In Rust, removing or\n432:A non-breaking public API extension does not require human authorization, but this document must\n433:describe the resulting public surface whenever the extension affects UI integration, agent-provider\n439:same patch as the code change.\n443:## Validation Expectations\n446:`AgentBackend` without depending on Codex-specific code. `tests/agent_provider_interface.rs` covers\n449:Controller and UI behavior should use `WorkLeafController`, `TerminalApp`, and `UiHarness` tests\n459:existing test suites under `tests/orchestrator_protocol.rs`, `tests/patching.rs`,\n460:`tests/reviews.rs`, `tests/linearize.rs`, and `tests/workspace.rs` provide the current coverage\n464:----- BEGIN FILE src/agent.rs -----\n473:pub use crate::agent_runtime::{AgentBackend, AgentShutdownHandle, AgentStreamEvent};\n476:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq, Ord, PartialOrd, Hash)]\n477:pub struct AgentId(String);\n479:impl AgentId {\n480:    pub fn new(value: impl Into<String>) -> Result<Self, AgentError> {\n484:            return Err(AgentError::InvalidAgentId(\n485:                \"agent id cannot be empty\".to_string(),\n492:            return Err(AgentError::InvalidAgentId(format!(\n493:                \"agent id `{trimmed}` cannot contain whitespace or control characters\"\n504:impl fmt::Display for AgentId {\n510:impl Serialize for AgentId {\n519:impl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for AgentId {\n529:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n530:pub enum AgentKind {\n535:impl AgentKind {\n544:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n545:pub struct AgentProfile {\n546:    pub kind: AgentKind,\n551:impl AgentProfile {\n553:        kind: AgentKind,\n566:            kind: AgentKind::Codex,\n568:            default_feature: \"user-agent\".to_string(),\n573:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n576:    Agent,\n581:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n596:#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n597:pub struct AgentLaunch {\n598:    pub id: AgentId,\n599:    pub kind: AgentKind,\n604:impl AgentLaunch {\n606:        id: AgentId,