{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a04350-cccf-7010-9e54-b8d50e78458b","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit f53e1da078a31726b40613db2397f588f2fa2080.\nI received the `src/ui.rs` and HTTP controller bundle. I’m checking whether the new `Done` status actually produces the requested terminal behavior and whether remote/event consumers still receive enough status to render correctly.\n\nThe UI row data model only has `ready`; clearing ready leaves the chat selectable, while setting ready highlights it. I’m checking whether “yes closes it” was expected as hiding/removing the chat or just clearing the highlight before I decide whether that is a behavioral finding.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- `src/workspace.rs:742`: `append_agent_line` drops duplicate transcript lines, but `request_feature_done_confirmation` at `src/workspace.rs:782` always appends the same `\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"` string after each `ReviewComplete` path at `src/workspace.rs:711`. After a user answers `no`, or answers `yes` then later reopens and completes another review, the session status is set back to awaiting confirmation but the new prompt is not appended at the end of the chat. The chat can be highlighted without visibly asking the required yes/no question for the latest review cycle.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification. The patch affects agent-facing review completion and terminal chat behavior, but the recorded validation only shows `cargo test --test ui_harness --test workspace`. This would be resolved by reporting an exact real configured backend scenario and visible result for review completion prompting, `yes` local close, and later chat reopen, or by reporting the exact pre-agent blocker from the required bounded smoke check.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","text_elements":[]}]},"threadId":"01a04347-4439-7793-843e-fa41147c6505","turnId":"01a04350-ca46-7472-b1da-0701754beca0","startedAtMs":1787835763919},"emittedAtMs":1787835763919}
{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a04350-cccf-7010-9e54-b8d50e78458b","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit f53e1da078a31726b40613db2397f588f2fa2080.\nI received the `src/ui.rs` and HTTP controller bundle. I’m checking whether the new `Done` status actually produces the requested terminal behavior and whether remote/event consumers still receive enough status to render correctly.\n\nThe UI row data model only has `ready`; clearing ready leaves the chat selectable, while setting ready highlights it. I’m checking whether “yes closes it” was expected as hiding/removing the chat or just clearing the highlight before I decide whether that is a behavioral finding.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- `src/workspace.rs:742`: `append_agent_line` drops duplicate transcript lines, but `request_feature_done_confirmation` at `src/workspace.rs:782` always appends the same `\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"` string after each `ReviewComplete` path at `src/workspace.rs:711`. After a user answers `no`, or answers `yes` then later reopens and completes another review, the session status is set back to awaiting confirmation but the new prompt is not appended at the end of the chat. The chat can be highlighted without visibly asking the required yes/no question for the latest review cycle.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification. The patch affects agent-facing review completion and terminal chat behavior, but the recorded validation only shows `cargo test --test ui_harness --test workspace`. This would be resolved by reporting an exact real configured backend scenario and visible result for review completion prompting, `yes` local close, and later chat reopen, or by reporting the exact pre-agent blocker from the required bounded smoke check.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","text_elements":[]}]},"threadId":"01a04347-4439-7793-843e-fa41147c6505","turnId":"01a04350-ca46-7472-b1da-0701754beca0","completedAtMs":1787835763919},"emittedAtMs":1787835763919}
