t writes still require `@work-leaf edit`.\nBundled files:\n- src/terminal_app.rs (fnv64:25dc74bb7b8daeba; bytes:42898)\n- tests/terminal_ui.rs (fnv64:0fd356411cefa671; bytes:10690)\n\n6 agent:\nThe extra bundle has the terminal app and lower-level UI tests. I’m checking whether the real terminal adapter already has a clipboard/output path so the visual-mode action can be wired consistently instead of only existing in the harness.\n\nThere’s a shared `TerminalAppCore` for local and remote terminal apps. I’m reading its input/rendering paths now so the copy behavior can be represented as a controller-visible status line without adding platform clipboard dependencies.\n\n@work-leaf read src/cli.rs\n\n7 user:\nwork-leaf file text\nExact file text is in an orchestrator context bundle instead of this chat to keep the agent session compact.\nContext bundle: /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/context-bundles/orchestrator-1815816-0/bundle-4.md\nYou may read this temporary bundle file for the exact mediated file text. Do not edit the bundle; project writes still require `@work-leaf edit`.\nBundled files:\n- src/cli.rs (fnv64:22710fff93cc0275; bytes:50711)\n\n8 agent:\nI have the CLI bundle too. I’m checking the chat transcript formatter because visual mode needs a stable “pane text” source for right-pane selections, including the live `chat> ` input line.\n\n@work-leaf edit ADD vim-style visual selection so focused terminal panes can highlight and yank text\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: src/ui.rs\n@@\n use std::{\n-    cell::Cell,\n+    cell::{Cell, RefCell},\n     path::PathBuf,\n     time::{Duration, Instant},\n };\n@@\n pub enum UiMode {\n     Command,\n     Insert,\n     Prompt,\n+    Visual,\n+    VisualLine,\n+    VisualBlock,\n }\n@@\n pub enum UiKey {\n     Char(char),\n     Esc,\n     CtrlW,\n+    CtrlV,\n     Up,\n     Down,\n     Left,\n     Right,\n@@\n struct PromptView {\n     line: String,\n     curso