{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a04353-549c-72f2-97b5-31811d3c7ed8","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The original agent has responded to the findings for commit f53e1da078a31726b40613db2397f588f2fa2080.\n@work-leaf read src/workspace.rs tests/workspace.rs src/terminal_app.rs\n\norchestrator:\nsent file text to user-3: src/terminal_app.rs, src/workspace.rs, tests/workspace.rs\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\nI’m going to fix the duplicate-prompt issue first by looking at the applied controller code and tests in the bundle. The verification finding is separate; after the code fix and focused validation I’ll run or report the bounded real-agent smoke scenario instead of changing code for that.\n\nThe current applied code confirms the reviewer’s first finding: duplicate transcript suppression can hide later identical confirmation prompts. I’m changing the confirmation line to include the reviewed commit hash, which makes each review cycle visibly distinct while preserving the same yes/no instruction.\n\nI’m also adding a regression that runs two reviewed cycles for the same patch agent and verifies two visible yes/no prompts are present. That catches the exact path from `ReviewComplete` through `append_agent_line` where duplicate suppression previously hid the later prompt.\n\n@work-leaf edit FIX repeated review confirmation prompts so each completed review visibly asks yes/no\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: src/workspace.rs\n@@\n                 for review in results {\n                     self.record_review_result(review);\n                     self.append_agent_line(&review.commit.agent_id, format!(\"review: {text}\"));\n-                    self.request_feature_done_confirmation(&review.commit.agent_id);\n+                    self.request_feature_done_confirmation(review);\n                 }\n             }\n@@\n-    fn request_feature_done_confirmation(&mut self, agent_id: &AgentId) {\n+    fn request_feature_done_confirmation(&mut self, review: &ReviewResult) {\n+        let reviewed_hash = review\n+            .commit\n+            .hash\n+            .get(..12)\n+            .unwrap_or(review.commit.hash.as_str());\n         self.append_agent_line(\n-            agent_id,\n-            \"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\".to_string(),\n+            &review.commit.agent_id,\n+            format!(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no (reviewed {reviewed_hash})\"),\n         );\n         self.set_session_status(\n-            agent_id,\n+            &review.commit.agent_id,\n             WorkLeafSessionStatus::AwaitingFeatureDoneConfirmation,\n         );\n     }\n*** Update File: tests/workspace.rs\n@@\n     assert!(\n         patch_agent\n             .lines\n             .iter()\n-            .any(|line| line == \"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\")\n+            .any(|line| line.starts_with(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"))\n     );\n@@\n     assert!(backend.sends().iter().any(|(target, prompt)| {\n         target == &reviewer_id\n             && prompt.contains(\"Review the full patch scope\")\n             && prompt.contains(\"after second\")\n     }));\n+    let snapshot = controller.snapshot();\n+    let patch_agent = snapshot.session(&agent_id).expect(\"patch agent exists\");\n+    assert_eq!(\n+        patch_agent\n+            .lines\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|line| line.starts_with(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"))\n+            .count(),\n+        2,\n+        \"each completed review cycle should append a visible confirmation prompt\"\n+    );\n }\n*** End Patch\n@work-leaf end\n\norchestrator:\nsent patch diagnostics to user-3: tests/workspace.rs\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\nThe failed hunk was only the regression insertion point in `tests/workspace.rs`; the source hunk and first assertion context are still usable. I’m tightening the test insertion context to the exact repeated-review test body from the bundle.\n\n@work-leaf edit FIX repeated review confirmation prompts so each completed review visibly asks yes/no\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: src/workspace.rs\n@@\n                 for review in results {\n                     self.record_review_result(review);\n                     self.append_agent_line(&review.commit.agent_id, format!(\"review: {text}\"));\n-                    self.request_feature_done_confirmation(&review.commit.agent_id);\n+                    self.request_feature_done_confirmation(review);\n                 }\n             }\n@@\n-    fn request_feature_done_confirmation(&mut self, agent_id: &AgentId) {\n+    fn request_feature_done_confirmation(&mut self, review: &ReviewResult) {\n+        let reviewed_hash = review\n+            .commit\n+            .hash\n+            .get(..12)\n+            .unwrap_or(review.commit.hash.as_str());\n         self.append_agent_line(\n-            agent_id,\n-            \"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\".to_string(),\n+            &review.commit.agent_id,\n+            format!(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no (reviewed {reviewed_hash})\"),\n         );\n         self.set_session_status(\n-            agent_id,\n+            &review.commit.agent_id,\n             WorkLeafSessionStatus::AwaitingFeatureDoneConfirmation,\n         );\n     }\n*** Update File: tests/workspace.rs\n@@\n     assert!(\n         patch_agent\n             .lines\n             .iter()\n-            .any(|line| line == \"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\")\n+            .any(|line| line.starts_with(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"))\n     );\n@@\n     assert!(backend.sends().iter().any(|(target, prompt)| {\n         target == &agent_id && prompt == \"please reopen this feature\"\n     }));\n }\n \n+#[test]\n+fn controller_appends_each_feature_done_prompt_after_repeated_reviews() {\n+    let root = git_repo(\"workspace-repeated-feature-done-confirmation\");\n+    fs::write(root.join(\"README.md\"), \"before\\n\").unwrap();\n+    git(&root, [\"add\", \"README.md\"]);\n+    git(&root, [\"commit\", \"-m\", \"ADD initial readme fixture\"]);\n+    let backend = FakeBackend::new([\n+        \"first patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-before\\n+after first\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\n+        \"summary: README changes to after first\",\n+        \"NO_FINDINGS\",\n+        \"second patch\\n@work-leaf patch update readme again\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-after first\\n+after second\\n@work-leaf end\\n@work-leaf done\",\n+        \"summary: README changes to after second\",\n+        \"NO_FINDINGS\",\n+    ]);\n+    let chat = CommandChat::new(root, backend).with_max_review_rounds(4);\n+    let mut controller = WorkLeafController::new(chat);\n+\n+    let agent_id = controller.create_agent(\"update readme\").unwrap();\n+    assert!(controller.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(2)));\n+    controller.send_message(&agent_id, \"no\").unwrap();\n+    controller\n+        .send_message(&agent_id, \"make the second update\")\n+        .unwrap();\n+    assert!(controller.wait_for_idle(Duration::from_secs(2)));\n+\n+    let snapshot = controller.snapshot();\n+    let patch_agent = snapshot.session(&agent_id).expect(\"patch agent exists\");\n+    assert_eq!(\n+        patch_agent\n+            .lines\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|line| line.starts_with(\"work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no\"))\n+            .count(),\n+        2,\n+        \"each completed review cycle should append a visible confirmation prompt\"\n+    );\n+}\n+\n #[test]\n fn controller_does_not_start_review_until_patch_agent_reports_done() {\n*** End Patch\n@work-leaf end\n\norchestrator:\napplied patch from user-3: FIX repeated review confirmation prompts so each completed review visibly asks yes/no; commit=3ed1cda32ea42f508475489637c0ce7d86c1f5fd; files=src/workspace.rs, tests/workspace.rs\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\n@work-leaf locks run target Cargo.lock -- cargo test --test workspace controller_appends_each_feature_done_prompt_after_repeated_reviews controller_yes_closes_reviewed_feature_and_later_chat_reopens_it -- --exact\n\norchestrator:\nran command for user-3: status=1 paths=Cargo.lock, target command=cargo test --test workspace controller_appends_each_feature_done_prompt_after_repeated_reviews controller_yes_closes_reviewed_feature_and_later_chat_reopens_it -- --exact\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\n@work-leaf locks run target Cargo.lock -- cargo test --test workspace feature_done\n\norchestrator:\nran command for user-3: status=0 paths=Cargo.lock, target command=cargo test --test workspace feature_done\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\n@work-leaf locks run target -- sh -lc \"printf 'Reply exactly with WORK_LEAF_REAL_AGENT_OK and do not modify files.\\n' | codex --cd \\\"$PWD\\\" --sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval never exec --color never --json -\"\n\norchestrator:\nran command for user-3: status=0 paths=target command=sh -lc \"printf 'Reply exactly with WORK_LEAF_REAL_AGENT_OK and do not modify files.\\n' | codex --cd \\\"$PWD\\\" --sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval never exec --color never --json -\"\n\nagent follow-up from user-3:\nReal-agent verification: ran the required bounded Codex smoke command in read-only/no-approval mode; it started thread `01a04353-010f-7921-bb6b-d21434e0d8e4` and returned `WORK_LEAF_REAL_AGENT_OK`. Focused validation passed with `cargo test --test workspace feature_done`.\n\n@work-leaf done\n\norchestrator:\nagent user-3 reported done\n\nPlease check the patch again and reply with NO_FINDINGS if resolved, otherwise list remaining FINDINGS. The response may include code patches, verification evidence, real-agent smoke results, or an exact blocker; evaluate that evidence directly and do not require a code patch for a non-code finding. Documentation and plain-text updates are deferred to the linearize agent and must not be reported as remaining patch-agent findings.","text_elements":[]}]},"threadId":"01a0434e-39d0-76d2-840b-4bb14335d058","turnId":"01a04353-5460-70d0-812f-436a293d355c","startedAtMs":1787835929756},"emittedAtMs":1787835929756}
