{"method":"turn/completed","params":{"threadId":"01a04352-f47e-7d50-8555-36919dab4f2b","turn":{"id":"01a04355-a805-7052-8362-de7490e29ecc","items":[{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_067fd4bb33581155016a9037198c4c87d2b1c6f210184e80f2","text":"FINDINGS\n\n- `src/ui.rs:980`: left-pane visual mode uses `control_selected` as the rendered row, but `left_pane_lines()` also inserts metadata rows for files and agent links at `src/ui.rs:1027` and `src/ui.rs:1041`. When the focused selection is an agent after another agent with metadata, `v`/`V`/Ctrl-V starts on the previous agent’s metadata instead of the focused agent row, so yanking copies the wrong text. The selected agent needs to be mapped to its actual rendered left-pane row.\n\n- `src/ui.rs:386`: mouse clicks are handled before the visual-mode key path, and `handle_mouse_click` at `src/ui.rs:1134` changes mode/focus without clearing `visual_selection`. Rendering still applies `visual_selection_range` at `src/ui.rs:1081`, so clicking out of visual mode leaves stale highlighted text even though the UI is no longer in visual mode. Clear the visual selection when mouse input exits visual mode.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification: the source context only shows `cargo test visual --all-targets --all-features` passing. This patch changes terminal chat/pane behavior, so the review evidence needs either an exact real-agent scenario and visible result, or the exact pre-agent blocker from the bounded Codex smoke workflow.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null}],"itemsView":"summary","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1787836082,"completedAt":1787836192,"durationMs":109775}},"emittedAtMs":1787836192009}
