{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a04357-5541-7a10-b6ac-585b7e6219cc","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit 958d0887669e2c5fa20adce9aad75a1128a71b7b.\nI found one concrete behavior issue in the cumulative patch and I’m checking exact file-relative line numbers from the mediated bundle now. After that I’ll return the review in the required `FINDINGS` format.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- `src/ui.rs:980`: left-pane visual mode uses `control_selected` as the rendered row, but `left_pane_lines()` also inserts metadata rows for files and agent links at `src/ui.rs:1027` and `src/ui.rs:1041`. When the focused selection is an agent after another agent with metadata, `v`/`V`/Ctrl-V starts on the previous agent’s metadata instead of the focused agent row, so yanking copies the wrong text. The selected agent needs to be mapped to its actual rendered left-pane row.\n\n- `src/ui.rs:386`: mouse clicks are handled before the visual-mode key path, and `handle_mouse_click` at `src/ui.rs:1134` changes mode/focus without clearing `visual_selection`. Rendering still applies `visual_selection_range` at `src/ui.rs:1081`, so clicking out of visual mode leaves stale highlighted text even though the UI is no longer in visual mode. Clear the visual selection when mouse input exits visual mode.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification: the source context only shows `cargo test visual --all-targets --all-features` passing. This patch changes terminal chat/pane behavior, so the review evidence needs either an exact real-agent scenario and visible result, or the exact pre-agent blocker from the bounded Codex smoke workflow.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","text_elements":[]}]},"threadId":"01a04347-1d9c-76c2-ac69-dc636dc8b712","turnId":"01a04357-550b-7d81-8fb1-5a851b13b93d","startedAtMs":1787836192065},"emittedAtMs":1787836192065}
{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a04357-5541-7a10-b6ac-585b7e6219cc","clientId":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit 958d0887669e2c5fa20adce9aad75a1128a71b7b.\nI found one concrete behavior issue in the cumulative patch and I’m checking exact file-relative line numbers from the mediated bundle now. After that I’ll return the review in the required `FINDINGS` format.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- `src/ui.rs:980`: left-pane visual mode uses `control_selected` as the rendered row, but `left_pane_lines()` also inserts metadata rows for files and agent links at `src/ui.rs:1027` and `src/ui.rs:1041`. When the focused selection is an agent after another agent with metadata, `v`/`V`/Ctrl-V starts on the previous agent’s metadata instead of the focused agent row, so yanking copies the wrong text. The selected agent needs to be mapped to its actual rendered left-pane row.\n\n- `src/ui.rs:386`: mouse clicks are handled before the visual-mode key path, and `handle_mouse_click` at `src/ui.rs:1134` changes mode/focus without clearing `visual_selection`. Rendering still applies `visual_selection_range` at `src/ui.rs:1081`, so clicking out of visual mode leaves stale highlighted text even though the UI is no longer in visual mode. Clear the visual selection when mouse input exits visual mode.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification: the source context only shows `cargo test visual --all-targets --all-features` passing. This patch changes terminal chat/pane behavior, so the review evidence needs either an exact real-agent scenario and visible result, or the exact pre-agent blocker from the bounded Codex smoke workflow.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","text_elements":[]}]},"threadId":"01a04347-1d9c-76c2-ac69-dc636dc8b712","turnId":"01a04357-550b-7d81-8fb1-5a851b13b93d","completedAtMs":1787836192065},"emittedAtMs":1787836192065}
