g command changes remain. The orchestrator returns the current tracked\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:404:`@work-leaf done`; patch application alone is not a review-readiness signal. Each patch agent uses a\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:409:the reviewer reports no findings, the review chat can be marked done by the user.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:427:9. The orchestrator returns a patch-applied continuation prompt when the patch agent has not reported\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:428:   done.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:430:    tracked command output through the patch protocol, and reports `@work-leaf done` when the patch is\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:437:15. If the review agent reports no findings, the user can mark the review chat as done.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:446:The example below shows the default read-permission interaction, not the raw terminal rendering.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:538:the user can mark the review chat as done and proceed toward linearization.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:544:- `src/agent.rs::PromptPolicy`: injects file-access rules into agent prompts.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:545:- `src/agent.rs::ReadPermission`: selects orchestrator-mediated or direct filesystem read prompts.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:556:  classification, sends, done, stale updates, and follow-up routing.\ndocs/orchestrator-file-workflow.md:567:- `src/terminal_app.rs::RemoteTerminalApp`: renders the CLI terminal UI through the HTTP controller\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},"threadId":"01a0435a-7a39-7370-aa21-a3cfb67db9cd","turnId":"01a0435a-7a8e-76b2-a3d1-d02fdf4c0b0a","completedAtMs":1787836470879},"emittedAtMs":1787836470880}
